id "dd37bb79-8cc2-5705-a5b2-95b0e7ce6d40" :question/math-academy-id "q-107131" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${0,1,t}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{2}[t]$\n- $2-t$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${0,1,t}$\n- ${0,1,t}$ is a basis of ${R}_{2}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1+0\\cdot t=0,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the first coefficient is nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent. In general, any set that contains a zero-vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n2-t=0\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot t.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107131/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107131"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94847/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9744c98b-0d9b-5426-bb5a-fef9b33369e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94847/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "35f4d458-84be-5e10-af86-a8f1e3e551fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94847/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "650b6c2d-65ec-5036-8587-8629c7a303f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94847/selection/5b26512916f